ieicr rdawr      0x0            0x0            ok   st.b 0x5a then ld.bu at IEICR in ONE session reads 0x0: the write was DECLINED (a backed accept reads 0x5a)
ieerr rdawr      0x0            0x0            ok   the same at IEERR (0x28), the write-to-clear class whose cased sibling SCCERR clears on write
sccerr rdawr     0x0            0x0            ok   CONTROL: the CASED write-to-clear sibling reads 0x0 under either disposition -- makes the two rows above attributable
latch sameoff    1              1              ok   two writes to one offset announce ONCE: an unlatched arm prints 2
latch twooff     1              2              FAIL two offsets announce TWICE: a single whole-arm latch bit prints 1
latch rw one     1              1              ok   a write then a read at ONE offset announce once: the latch is per offset, not per direction
